{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>\"And I sent to tell my lord\"</b> — to inform him that I am coming to you to find favor in your eyes, that I am whole with you and seek your love — this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Genesis 32:6). That is to say, it is not referred back to what precedes it, but rather one should read: \"And I sent to tell my lord that I am coming to find favor in your eyes and to do all that my lord commands.\" But it is more correct to refer it back to what precedes: \"And I sent to tell my lord\" — that I have wealth, possessions, and honor, to do with them your desire and will. He hints that he will send him a gift from them, or that he may take for himself from them whatever he desires. And so he said later (Genesis 33:8): \"What do you mean by all this camp that I have encountered? And he said, To find favor in the eyes of my lord.\""], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:38:49.597116104Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}